I LIKE both these suggestions!  I just saw someone else ascend with 967 
hit points due to many, many repeated applications of the cursed Bell of
Opening.  I've also seen another character that was so pumped up from 
this abuse that he started to read cursed scrolls of genocide and summoned
_Archons_ just for fun.  (And said character generally had about 500 hp
left afterward...)  An object of summon wraiths with infinite charges is 
just too powerful.

Polypiling is also still too powerful...  even with stuff vibrating away
and golems showing up.

There is one other suggestion I'd like to make.  NetHack is too easy at
high levels.  Personally, every character that I've gotten to the Castle
has made it to demigod(ess)hood.  So, make the monsters tougher at high
levels!  I welcome the presence of nasties like shades and archons just
because they make the game more challenging.  Also, I suggest:

*  Making things like Nazgul and Balrogs, which are _really_ tough in
   fantasy stories, tougher.  Say, as bad as minotaurs or even Archons.
   Lawful characters often don't get attacked by Archons (which are
   also lawful).  Why should they have it easy?

*  Make the L class un-genocideable.  Now that would be annoying.

*  Dragons are tougher in 3.1.  Good idea, but I think they should be
   still more powerful.  Remember, dragons are HUGE.  Or, maybe they
   could simply make more categories based on age, with the current 
   dragon stats being a mature dragon, and ancient dragon = Bad news.

*  Make the @'s on the astral plane (especially the other demigods) a
   lot tougher.  I looked at them with a stethoscope.  Wimps.  They 
   couldn't even clean out the castle, let alone deal with the Wiz!

Just my $0.02
